    "research": {
      "notes": "**1. Guidance and results**\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal turned up in the window. Q3 results are due before the open on Nov 3, 2026. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.shopify.com/news/shopify-q3-2026-financial-advisory\n- The latest results and guidance fall before the window. \nQ2 results on Aug 5 showed 34% revenue growth and an 18% FCF margin.\n — 2026-08-05 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001594805/000159480526000046/exhibit991pressreleaseq220.htm\n- \nA Stifel survey of 30 respondents points to growth accelerating to about 35% in Q3, against guidance of low-30s percent.\n That is an analyst expectation, not company guidance. — 2026-10-14 — https://it.investing.com/news/analyst-ratings/stifel-alza-il-target-su-shopify-grazie-alle-aspettative-di-crescita-93CH-3587483\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- \nJP Morgan (Smilek) raised its target to $200 from $185 and kept Overweight.\n — 2026-10-06 — https://www.benzinga.com/stock/SHOP/ratings?nid=43636620\n- \nSeaport Global raised its target to $180 from $175 (Buy).\n — 2026-10-08 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/shop/forecast\n- \nCantor Fitzgerald (Mathivanan) raised its target to $158 from $145 and stayed Neutral.\n — 2026-10-12 — https://www.benzinga.com/stock/SHOP/ratings?nid=43636620\n- \nBaird raised its target to $190 from $160 and reiterated Outperform.\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.defenseworld.net/2026/10/15/shopify-nasdaqshop-given-new-190-00-price-target-at-robert-w-baird.html\n- \nWedbush (Arounian) maintained Outperform with a $176 target.\n — 2026-09-23 — https://www.benzinga.com/stock/SHOP/ratings?nid=43636620\n- \nMizuho kept Outperform and a $180 target.\n The article is dated Oct 12 and doesn't give the date of the call. — date unknown — https://www.timothysykes.com/news/shopify-inc-shop-news-2026_10_12/\n- \nBMO moved its target to $165 from $160 (Buy).\n — date unknown — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/shop/forecast\n- Consensus target figures differ by source:\n  - \nMarketBeat: $175.37.\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/SHOP/forecast/\n  - \nBenzinga: $172.\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.benzinga.com/stock/SHOP/ratings?nid=43636620\n- I found no upgrades, downgrades or initiations inside the window. The most recent ones, from July and August, fall outside it.\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- I found nothing new or material in the window. The Briskin v. Shopify California privacy class action is the main known case. \nBloomberg Law reported Shopify must face the proposed class action.\n That article is about 75 days old, so it predates the window, and its event date isn't given. — date unknown — https://news.bloomberglaw.com/litigation/shopify-user-advances-lawsuit-over-collection-of-consumer-data\n- \nMLex reported a federal judge dismissed a related privacy suit.\n — 2026-01-22 (publication date; outside the window) — https://www.mlex.com/mlex/articles/2432858/privacy-suit-against-shopify-narrowed-by-us-judge\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- Nothing material found. Shopify serves millions of merchants, and I found no sign of reliance on a few customers. \nThe 10-Q names Aldo, BarkBox, Carrier, Meta, Vuori, SKIMS and Supreme as notable merchants.\n — 2026-06-30 (period end) — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001594805/000159480526000047/shop-20260630.htm\n\n**5. Insider activity**\nI found no open-market Form 4 purchases. What I found are Rule 144 sale notices.\n- Four officers filed Form 144 notices within about a week (Sept 18–25), mostly for sales tied to RSU vesting. That looks clustered, but most of it is tax-cover selling.\n- Finkelstein: \nnotice covers 10,131 shares tied to RSUs and 172,050 shares tied to RSUs and options, over three months from Sept 19.\n \nSome sales fall under a 10b5-1 plan adopted Nov 14, 2025, and some cover taxes.\n — 2026-09-18 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/144-shopify-inc-sec-filing-3f691b7fc8e8.html and https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1594805/000159480526000057/xsl144X01/primary_doc.xml\n- Hertz: \n11,171 shares, about $1.44M, tied to RSUs vesting Sept 19, to cover taxes and fees.\n — 2026-09-18 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/144-shopify-inc-sec-filing-346208e6aac0.html\n- Niehaus: \nup to 1,537 shares (about $198K) over a window starting Sept 19.\n — 2026-09-18 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/144-shopify-inc-sec-filing-d3cbe09ba14f.html\n- Hoffmeister: \nplanned sale of 6,152 shares, about $893K.\n \nThe sale is linked to RSU-vesting taxes and fees, starting Sept 26.\n — 2026-09-25 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/144-shopify-inc-sec-filing-e03f5b8a7fa4.html\n- Hoffmeister also sold \n11,647 shares on Sept 14 for about $1.54M.\n That is one day before the window opens. — 2026-09-14 — same URL\n- Lütke: his notice lists \n46,758 shares tied to a Sept 9 RSU vest\n. \nFuture sales are to be made under 10b5-1 plans adopted Dec 8, 2025.\n The filing date is about 40 days before today, so it may fall just before the window. — 2026-09-09 (RSU vest) — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/144-shopify-inc-sec-filing-b70e74bfedea.html and https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/SHOP/\n\n**6. Product and competitive news**\n- Canvas: \na generative-AI visual design workspace for building a custom store.\n It is listed on Shopify's press page. — 2026-10-01 — https://commonthreadco.com/blogs/coachs-corner/every-shopify-update-in-2026-updated-weekly and https://www.shopify.com/investors/press-releases\n- WebMCP checkout: \nlaunched for all eligible merchants, including Shop Pay.\n \nAn Instinct partnership was announced the same day.\n — 2026-09-28 — https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/28/shopify-opens-checkout-to-browser-based-ai-agents/\n- Meta's Muse agent: \ncan check out on Shopify stores using",
